## Core Interfaces

### MapState
```typescript
interface MapState {
  isZoomed: boolean   // Currently viewing a region
  isLoading: boolean  // Map assets loading
  isFrozen: boolean   // Stops animations (for scroll transition)
  isPaused: boolean   // Completely stops rendering
}
```

### UseMapReturn
```typescript
interface UseMapReturn {
  state: Ref<MapState>
  init: (container: HTMLElement) => void
  dispose: () => void
  zoomOut: () => void
  freeze: () => void
  unfreeze: () => void
  setScrollZoom: (progress: number) => void
  pause: () => void
  resume: () => void
}
```

---

## Module Details

### 1. index.ts - Main Orchestrator

**Key Responsibilities:**
- Vue composable entry point
- Three.js scene setup (scene, camera, renderer, lights)
- Animation loop ([animate()](file:///c:/Users/Xensa/Desktop/tour-nuxt/app/composables/useMap/index.ts#203-260))
- Event handling (mouse, click, resize)
- Resource disposal

**Internal State:**
```typescript
// Vue Refs
const state = ref<MapState>({...})
const isZoomAnimating = ref(false)
const zoomedCamPos = ref<CameraPosition>({...})

// Plain objects (no reactivity for performance)
const zoomBlend = { value: 0 }

// Three.js objects
let scene, camera, renderer
let combinedMapGroup, fogGroup, gridGroup, labelsGroup

// Data arrays
const interactablePoints: THREE.Group[] = []  // Markers
const fogParticles: THREE.Sprite[] = []
const gridLines: THREE.Line[] = []
const cityLabels: CityLabel[] = []
```

**Key Functions:**
| Function | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| [init(container)](file:///c:/Users/Xensa/Desktop/tour-nuxt/app/composables/useMap/index.ts#263-395) | Sets up scene, loads map, starts animation |
| [animate()](file:///c:/Users/Xensa/Desktop/tour-nuxt/app/composables/useMap/index.ts#203-260) | Main render loop (60fps) |
| [triggerZoomToRegion()](file:///c:/Users/Xensa/Desktop/tour-nuxt/app/composables/useMap/index.ts#182-200) | Zooms camera to clicked region |
| [highlightRegionMeshes()](file:///c:/Users/Xensa/Desktop/tour-nuxt/app/composables/useMap/index.ts#126-181) | Applies grid shader to region |
| [dispose()](file:///c:/Users/Xensa/Desktop/tour-nuxt/app/composables/useMap/index.ts#396-462) | Cleans up all Three.js resources |

---

### 2. camera.ts - Camera Controls

**Exports:**
```typescript
zoomIn(camera, targetPoint, tweenGroup, ...) → void
zoomOutCamera(camera, tweenGroup, ...) → void
updateParallax(camera, mouseCurrent, ...) → void
```

**Parallax States:**
1. **Standard** - Mouse moves camera slightly (~50px offset)
2. **Zoomed** - Subtle movement when viewing region (~20px offset)
3. **Blending** - Smooth transition from zoom to overview

---

### 3. loader.ts - SVG Map Loader

**Process:**
1. Fetches `/map.svg`
2. Parses SVG groups (`<g id="uz">`, `<g id="kz">`, etc.)
3. Creates `ExtrudeGeometry` for each path
4. Applies different materials:
   - **Uzbekistan**: Gold with custom grid shader
   - **Sea**: Blue, semi-transparent
   - **Neighbors**: White/gray

**Grid Shader:**
- Custom [onBeforeCompile](file:///c:/Users/Xensa/Desktop/tour-nuxt/app/composables/useMap/loader.ts#99-161) shader modification
- Blends grid texture on hover/selection
- Uses world-space UVs rotated 45°

---

### 4. labels.ts - City Labels

**CityLabel Structure:**
```typescript
interface CityLabel {
  group: THREE.Group      // Container
  textSprite: THREE.Sprite // Label text
  line: THREE.Line        // Leader line (elbow style)
  markerRef: THREE.Group  // Associated marker
  regionId: string
  isVisible: boolean
  targetOpacity: number
}
```

**Label Directions:**
- `top-right` - Diagonal up-right → horizontal right
- `bottom-right` - Diagonal down-right → horizontal right
- `top-left` - Diagonal up-left → horizontal left
- `bottom-left` - Diagonal down-left → horizontal left

**Visibility Logic:**
- Proximity-based: labels show when cursor is within `revealRadius` (150px)
- Zoom mode: only selected label visible (scaled 1.8x)

---

### 5. markers.ts - Region Markers

**Marker Structure:**
```
THREE.Group
├── SphereGeometry (center point)
├── TorusGeometry (static ring)
└── TorusGeometry (ripple animation)
```

**Ripple Animation:**
- Expands from 1x to 1.5x radius
- Border thickness grows (0.1 → 1.5)
- Opacity fades (0.7 → 0)
- Loops continuously

---

### 6. grid.ts - Background Grid

**Grid Composition:**
- Background plane (8000x8000)
- Horizontal lines (spacing: 40px)
- Vertical lines (spacing: 40px)
- Diagonal lines (every other cell)

**Animation:**
- Random opacity pulsing (0.02 - 0.4)
- Wave-based sine modulation

---

